      "id": 1,
      "text": "Stockport's hatting legacy ended in 1997 after over 400 years, when Christy's and Wilson's factories closed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockport",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 18th century, Stockport housed one of the British Isles' first mechanised silk factories, sparking early textile industry growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stockport",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town's football club, Stockport County, is nicknamed The Hatters, a nod to its historic hatting industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
